   :statement "V1/C460 produced H1's falsifier on record: on wm-trace-2026-07-04 and 07-05 the enacted action differs from the recorded Q(pi) selection (rank-1 ungated; first passing lower-ranked candidate enacted). THE SCALE, corrected 2026-09-01 (claude-20 and claude-1 independently, form by form): the first pass read one form per file and reported it as the file. Reading each file with edn/read in a loop, 07-04 holds 38 records of which 37 record both a selection and a realized policy, and 07-05 holds 18 of which 13 do. In 50 of those 50 comparable records the enacted action DIFFERS from the selection; in none of them do they agree. The Lean hole enactedActionEqualsSelected (Holes.lean:6596) is therefore refuted as written and must not stay open as if undecided."
   :acceptance "Holes.lean: enactedActionEqualsSelected is closed by record as REFUTED (mkWitnessedClosed or the registry's refuted form, evidence C460, the two trace files named), and a restated hole is declared bounding when the paths agree. CONSTRAINT ON THE RESTATEMENT (claude-20, steward, 2026-09-01): do not write a hole softer than the evidence allows. 'The enacted action equals the selection whenever the rank-1 selection passes its act gate' may be stated as a BOUND to be tested, but NOT as a claim believed true -- on the two files we have, the selection and the enactment coincide in zero of fifty comparable records, so nothing on record supports the agreeing case. The restated hole must carry the 50/50 in its own text and its falsifier must point at these two files by name, so a later reader cannot mistake an untested bound for a confirmed one. TWO DECLARATIONS, NOT ONE EDIT (claude-1, reading this row 2026-09-01): the refuted declaration and the restated bound are separate -- that enactedActionEqualsSelected was falsified is itself a fact worth keeping in Lean, and overwriting it with the bound would lose the history the ledger otherwise preserves. If the seat writes it as one, that is a review finding. Owner wm-organization; falsifier 'a run in which the rank-1 selection passes its gate and a different action is enacted'; registered in mkHole; lake build passes; sha here."}
