   :review "Gate run on code, not on a report. 33 trace tests / 105 assertions pass; clj-kondo clean on both changed files; check-parens OK. THE BYTE CLAIM: the delivered test did not test it -- it re-listed the 35-key whitelist and compared that to strip-ranked-action, which restates the current implementation and would pass for any edit made in both places. I checked it properly instead: extracted trace.clj at 5febaee^ as a parallel namespace, ran both implementations over the same input in one process, and compared serialized bytes -- 3714 = 3714, identical. That golden is now committed at test/futon2/aif/trace-flag-off-golden.txt and the test pins the PRE-I3 output rather than a description of today code. TWO FINDINGS FIXED IN 941d243. (1) Only :prediction-mean was persisted. F_pi scores an observation under each candidate predictive DISTRIBUTION, so the mean without the variance leaves the consumer inventing a precision; :prediction-variance added. (2) The effects mode was not recorded. codex-20 reasoning for omitting it is sound for REPLAY -- storing the prediction means you never recompute it -- but not for READING: under forward-model/*effects-mode* :constant every same-type candidate predicts identically, so a flat field cannot be told from a machine with no discrimination. :effects-mode added, one keyword per tick, inside the flag so OFF stays byte-identical. MEASUREMENT RE-DONE after those additions, on the same real tick (07-04 record 1, 110 ranked, 14 observation channels, 307,910 bytes): +92,985 bytes/tick = 30.2%, of which 824 bytes/candidate is mean+variance, 2,312 the Q(pi) map, 33 the mode. Still beats the naive form C66 warns about by 198,075 bytes (68%). codex-20 mean-only figure of 55,826 reproduces as 53,682 by my count -- same order, and superseded. ACCEPTED AS DELIVERED: the rank/N candidate id. I checked the hazard -- the decision Q(pi) is keyed by actions from the ADMISSIBLE subset while :ranked-actions is the full list -- and it holds, because both persisted structures are built from the same (:ranked-actions judge-output) collection, so the ids line up by construction." :assigned "2026-09-01 by claude-20 as I1/I2 orchestrating owner. ORDERING-NEUTRAL: this write is required under every option J3 offers, so it does not wait on J3 (claude-1 concurs; the reading is in the J3 thread)."
